{
	"Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Sign-In from a New IP After MFA Reset",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Initial Access / T1078\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Sign-In from a New IP After MFA Reset\" or \"<ip>|Okta Sign-In from a New IP After MFA Reset\"\n\nA successful Okta session start for a user whose MFA factors were reset or deactivated (user.mfa.factor.reset_all / deactivate) in the previous 12 hours, from an IP address that was not used for the reset. An attacker who talks a helpdesk into an MFA reset, then signs in with stolen credentials, produces exactly this sequence.\n\nFalse positives: a user who resets MFA from one network and signs in from another (home vs office).\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/persistence_stolen_credentials_used_to_login_to_okta_account_after_mfa_reset/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/persistence_stolen_credentials_used_to_login_to_okta_account_after_mfa_reset.toml",
	"GUID": "d4af0ac9-8ba1-5394-a271-0aea6619cac3",
	"Labels": [
		"okta",
		"detection",
		"authentication-sessions",
		"initial-access",
		"T1078"
	],
